  "closed_findings": [
    {
      "id": "B1",
      "classification": "BLOCKER_CLOSED",
      "root_cause": "A failed inspect suppressed the stop attempt for an already known CID.",
      "fix": "close_known treats unreadable state as potentially running, attempts the fixed CID stop, separately checks final physical state, records initial inspect/stop failures, remains UNCONFIRMED when state cannot be established and continues all six owners.",
      "independent_counterexample": "Original containment-initial01.txt failed; exact same test passes in containment-final03.txt."
    },
    {
      "id": "B2",
      "classification": "BLOCKER_CLOSED",
      "root_cause": "Core metadata was not sufficient to bind the actual DSN; a wrong/copy Core or shadow DNS could yield a misplaced receipt.",
      "fix": "Worker URL and pgx parsing jointly require exact postgres URI host dpp-lifecycle307-808a6960-postgres, 5432, lifecycle307, fixture, nonempty password and only sslmode=disable, with no TLS/fallback. Host preparation verifies actual fixed Core name plus Docker Aliases/DNSNames, expected workspace/provider/incarnation/actor; active topology rejects another running owner with the fixed Core DNS name. Manifest includes a sanitized Core binding and the actual source-profile SHA, without emitting credentials.",
      "independent_counterexample": "Foreign-owner DNS shadow was admitted by preserved initial source (core-shadow-initial01.txt FAIL) and rejected by current source (core-shadow-final02.txt PASS). Parent host/Go DSN expansion tests independently rerun as part of final suites."
    },
    {
      "id": "B3",
      "classification": "BLOCKER_CLOSED",
      "root_cause": "Generic stdout-only call dropped the original stderr from a failed non-TTY helper when docker logs CLI itself succeeded.",
      "fix": "Dedicated owner_logs writes stdout/stderr separately with O_EXCL, sizes and raw SHA. Generic call/docker keep the original stdout bytes return contract; owner terminal gate checks both container and logs CLI exit codes.",
      "independent_counterexample": "Original owner-stderr-initial01.txt FAIL; unchanged counterexample passes owner-stderr-final02.txt with original stderr retained."
    }
  ],
  "other_required_path_review": [
    "Fresh audit ID and purpose are separate from the old execution; config rejects extra root/send fields and narrows source/workspace/provider/incarnation/actor/time/queue. New recovery profile carries only inspect credentials; root bootstrap has separate mounts and can enable only the exact inspector after all four users are disabled and frozen official MinIO policy semantics/no groups/single policy match.",
    "Worker verifies the original exact P1 CONFIRMED ACCEPTED observation and no previous absence, validates frozen bindings, checks seven retained versions by exact HEAD/protection and both complete namespace lists with P1 absent. Current native receipt keeps actual inspections and inventories; it explicitly does not claim a new bytes/SHA content read.",
    "New RequestRecovery work uses existing Core service and transactional Outbox. OnlyEventID filters before claim/lease mutation. Selected enqueuer, Asynq task ID and selected runner additionally require the exact new work/workspace. Separate Redis prevents consuming the old queue.",
    "Existing recovery service and per-call authority journal perform reads and append Core absence/finalization/cost facts. No DELETE/dispatch/Renew/hold mutation is reachable in the new mode. Original native attempt/observation/budgets/pins and old failure state are not rewritten.",
    "Before/after Core relation fingerprints restrict changed relations; whole-row hash multisets prove old appendable facts/obligations/cost rows remain present. Identity disable uses fresh readback independently from physical stopped/PID0 proof; failures never become a sealed PASS without all required evidence."
  ],
